{
  "about": "Rooms that live on another server (share claude/tinhat-server/MATRIX-FRONTEND-DESIGN.md B0/B1/B5, the must-fix round). Owned by the web (src/core/matrix/foreign.ts); the desktop's crates/app/src/testvectors/foreign-room.json is a byte-identical copy (foreign_room.rs). serverPart: the server part of a user id, a pre-v12 room id or an alias, '' for a v12 opaque room id or anything that is not a valid server name (a bracketed IPv6 literal must be a real IPv6 address, as Rust's Ipv6Addr reads it; a port is 1-65535). origin: the server of the m.room.create sender, null when the create event is missing or has no valid sender. managed: Tin Hat may change this room's power levels only when the create sender AND every v12 additional_creators entry are on my own server (exact match); a missing create event, a missing own server or a malformed additional_creators means no. via: the servers a join asks through: the link's via, then the space child's via, then the server part of the target (never anything for a v12 opaque id), then hints (the inviter's or the child event sender's server); '' and invalid names dropped, duplicates dropped, at most 3 (matrix-js-sdk sends only 3). plan: the one power-level write ensureWritable / ensure_writable may make: none in a room that isn't managed (foreign: on open AND on call join); else each requested type that is Tin Hat's own (dev.tinhat.*) or call membership, not already done this session, whose effective level (events[t], else state_default, else 50; an integer string like \"50\" (no whitespace) counts as its number, as older room versions allow) is above 0, lowered to 0, and only when I may edit power levels.",
